# A worktree is a second checkout of THIS repository living inside the first.
# Git knows that and skips them; prettier and eslint do not, so every tool run
# in the main checkout walked into every sibling branch's files. The symptom was
# `verify` failing in the main checkout with 169 style issues in code that was
# not being changed there — which made the main checkout the one place in this
# project where nothing could be committed at all.
#
# Each worktree formats and lints its own tree. Nothing is skipped; it is
# checked once, where it is being edited, instead of N times from N branches.
.claude/worktrees/
